---
import WikiLayout from '../../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import { PENDING } from '../../lib/pending';

const pending = `<strong class="pending">${PENDING}</strong>`;

const pages: Record<string, { title: string; description: string; body: string }> = {
	'como-chegar': {
		title: 'Getting here',
		description: 'How to reach Muimenta, where to park, and what to bring.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Muimenta is in Carballeda de Avia, Ourense. Always confirm your arrival time and meeting point with the team.</p>
<h2>Where we are</h2>
<p>The project spaces — community kitchen, housing module, social centre and coworking — are in the village itself. For GPS, search <em>Muimenta, Carballeda de Avia</em>. If it is your first time, agree the exact arrival point and the keys with Lucía, the local connector.</p>
<h2>By car</h2>
<ul>
<li>On a residency arrival: unload at the module, then leave the car at the <strong>social centre</strong> or the <strong>palco</strong>.</li>
<li>For busy <strong>events</strong>, park at the village <strong>water tank</strong> so the centre of the village stays clear.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Without a car</h2>
<p>There is no frequent bus to the door. If you arrive by train or bus, agree a pickup with the team or take a taxi or shared car from the nearest stop. We do not publish a fixed taxi number here until it is confirmed. Write to the team before you travel.</p>
<h2 id="pack-de-chegada">Arrival pack</h2>
<p>Bring:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Shampoo and soap.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Food</strong>, especially if you arrive outside shop hours.</li>
<li>An <strong>umbrella</strong>.</li>
<li>A <strong>swimsuit and a towel</strong> if you want the pool (poza) or the hot springs. Exact places are still open: see <a href="/en/vida-diaria/mobilidade/#lugares">Getting around</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Sheets and house towels</h3>
<p>It is not confirmed whether the house provides sheets and towels. Until the team says so, bring your own: ${pending}</p>
<h3>Bicycle and animals</h3>
<ul>
<li>Whether the project has bicycles, or where to get one: ${pending}</li>
<li>There are loose dogs in the village. Whether you can bring a pet: ${pending}</li>
</ul>
<h2>On arrival</h2>
<ol>
<li>Say you are on the way (project WhatsApp / Lucía).</li>
<li>Unload at the module and park at the social centre or the palco.</li>
<li>Collect the keys and walk through the spaces.</li>
<li>First day: shared life, neighbours’ privacy, and the rhythm of the house. Read <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">Co-living</a> and <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a>.</li>
</ol>`,
	},
	'casa/convivencia': {
		title: 'Co-living',
		description: 'First-day agreements, privacy, and the module-visit protocol.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Clear agreements on arrival: how we share spaces, how we protect neighbours’ privacy, and how the house keeps a healthy rhythm.</p>
<p>This is the co-living onboarding. We are in an activation phase, with few people here day to day. The agreements still apply — each presence is easy to feel.</p>
<h2>First-day agreements</h2>
<p>On the first day we walk through three things, slowly:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Shared life</strong> — kitchen, time, tasks, and leaving what you used ready for the next person.</li>
<li><strong>Neighbours’ privacy</strong> — the village is not a set. Do not enter houses, gardens or yards without an explicit invitation.</li>
<li><strong>The rhythm of the house</strong> — meals are not assumed to be shared, and the village calendar does not bend to your project.</li>
</ul>
<p>That day (or on the video call beforehand, if it is not closed yet) we also settle:</p>
<ul>
<li>A <strong>concrete project</strong>, not only an intention. You can join what is already happening. Do not impose your agenda on the village. See <a href="/en/residencias/expectativas/">Expectations</a>.</li>
<li>Who your contact person is, and the coordination channel (project WhatsApp).</li>
<li><strong>Explicit consent</strong> before publishing photos or videos of people.</li>
<li>The <a href="#visitas-modulos">module visit protocol</a>.</li>
<li>Before you commit to visits, workshops or public activities, <strong>check with the team</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote><p>“I will check with the team and get back to you.”</p></blockquote>
<p>That is the operational-neutrality line. It keeps Sende, Anceu and the connector aligned. Do not take on institutional commitments that are outside the residency.</p>
<h2 id="visitas-modulos">Visits to the modules</h2>
<p>Sometimes the rehabilitated module needs to be shown. That happens by protocol, so the building can be seen without breaking privacy. There are no improvised entries into rooms.</p>
<ul>
<li>There is <strong>notice beforehand</strong>.</li>
<li>A <strong>responsible person from the team</strong> opens. The visit always happens with that person.</li>
<li><strong>You can say no.</strong></li>
</ul>
<h2>Spaces and privacy</h2>
<ul>
<li>The <strong>community kitchen</strong> is the main place for shared life.</li>
<li>The <strong>housing module</strong> is private: not for group activities or open visits. See <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a>.</li>
<li>Respect neighbours. Do not assume you can enter houses, gardens or yards.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Daily rhythm</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Do not assume</strong> every meal is shared. Each person keeps their own rhythm, except for agreed gatherings.</li>
<li><strong>Shared dinners</strong> can have an agreed frequency (for example twice a week, in the Anceu style). Set that at the start.</li>
<li>Join everyday tasks in a way that is useful to you and to the neighbours.</li>
<li>A local host, when there is one, commits in the programme rules to a minimum of 1 hour a week — not daily tasks. Detail in <a href="/en/residencias/modelo/">The model</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Image, audio and publishing</h2>
<ul>
<li>Ask for <strong>explicit consent</strong> before publishing photos or videos of people. The same applies to audio and to QR content that involves people in the village.</li>
<li>If someone prefers not to appear, respect that even when it is part of your residency project.</li>
<li>Public project materials (posters, social channels) include the Xunta / Consellería de Emprego branding when it applies. Ask the team if you are unsure.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Flexibility and mutual care</h2>
<p>We look for flexible people, ready to join collective activities without forcing the village agenda. If something does not fit, say so early to the connector.</p>
<p>See also: <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a> · <a href="/en/casa/limpeza/">Cleaning</a> · <a href="/en/residencias/expectativas/">Expectations</a> · <a href="/en/como-chegar/#pack-de-chegada">Arrival pack</a>.</p>`,
	},
	'casa/espazos': {
		title: 'Spaces',
		description: 'Community kitchen, private module, two-storey social centre, and the windowed coworking.',
		body: `<p class="lede">The rehabilitated buildings have different uses. Using each one for what it is avoids friction.</p>
<h2>Community kitchen</h2>
<p>The <strong>main shared space</strong>: gatherings, MuiGastromenta cooking, vermouth, and most of the life between residents, team and neighbours.</p>
<ul>
<li>Basic kitchen equipment. Do not assume special tools.</li>
<li>Leave it clean and tidy.</li>
<li>Check with Lucía if you need it for a specific activity.</li>
<li>The large oven and the dishwasher are not for an ordinary day with few people. The rule is in <a href="/en/vida-diaria/comidas/#forno">Food</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Tableware</h2>
<p>Dishes currently move up and down between the community kitchen and the upper floor of the social centre, and pieces go missing in one place or the other. There is not yet a full set on each floor.</p>
<ul>
<li>Take tableware from the space where you will use it, and put it back there.</li>
<li>Do not assume both spaces have enough glasses, cups and plates.</li>
</ul>
<p>The team wants a basic duplicated set in the community kitchen and on the upper floor. Until that exists, use the rule above.</p>
<h2>Housing module</h2>
<p>The module is a <strong>private</strong> place to rest. It is not for group activities, open visits or workshops.</p>
<p>If it has to be shown, that follows the <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/#visitas-modulos">visit protocol</a>: notice beforehand, a responsible person from the team, and you can say no.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Shower:</strong> water seeps under the tray and the area stays wet, which can cause a smell. Review and repair are a priority for the team. If it gets worse, tell the connector.</div>
<h2>Social centre</h2>
<p>This is the <strong>two-storey</strong> building. It is for community events (openings, presentations, public activities). The upper floor is where there is more activity and the larger events. Use is coordinated with the team and, when it applies, with municipal services.</p>
<h2>Coworking</h2>
<p>This is the building with the <strong>large windows</strong>. It is for work, small meetings and entrepreneurship activities. Furniture and tableware are still being completed; ask what is actually there when you arrive.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Quick map:</strong> shared life and cooking in the community kitchen; rest in the module; open events in the social centre (two floors); work in the coworking (the windows).</div>
<p>See also: <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">Co-living</a> · <a href="/en/casa/limpeza/">Cleaning</a> · <a href="/en/vida-diaria/comidas/">Food</a>.</p>`,
	},
	'casa/limpeza': {
		title: 'Cleaning',
		description: 'Simple routines for cared-for shared spaces.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Shared spaces work when each person leaves what they used at least as ready as they found it.</p>
<h2>After using a shared space</h2>
<ul>
<li>Wash and put away the community-kitchen tableware.</li>
<li>Return glasses, cups and plates to the space where you took them (community kitchen or upper floor). There is not yet a duplicated set on each floor.</li>
<li>Wipe tables and surfaces after workshops or meals.</li>
<li>Take rubbish to the right bins.</li>
<li>Do not leave open food that will draw insects or damp.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Private module</h2>
<ul>
<li>Keep your room livable during the stay.</li>
<li>When you leave, the module should be clean and aired (see <a href="/en/antes-de-irte/">Before you leave</a>).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Events</h2>
<p>For larger gatherings, cleaning before and after is coordinated with the connector and, if it applies, with municipal support. Do not assume someone else will do it.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Damp:</strong> some spaces are sensitive to humidity. Air them with care and report problems (mould, leaks, broken parts). Water seeping under the module shower tray is a known issue: say if it gets worse.</div>`,
	},
	'vida-diaria/comidas': {
		title: 'Food',
		description: 'Meals, the large oven, and how shopping works.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Sharing a table is part of life in the village, but it is not a daily obligation. Agree it when you arrive.</p>
<h2>Basic principle</h2>
<p><strong>Do not assume</strong> every meal is collective. Each resident organises their own food (temporary residencies are unpaid and board is your own, according to the rules).</p>
<h2>Agreed dinners and gatherings</h2>
<ul>
<li>You can agree a frequency of <strong>shared dinners</strong> (for example twice a week), close to the rhythm of other spaces in the network such as Anceu.</li>
<li>MuiGastromenta gatherings have their own logic: see <a href="/en/vida-diaria/muigastromenta/">MuiGastromenta</a>.</li>
<li>At open events, food is coordinated with the team.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Community kitchen</h2>
<p>Use the community kitchen to cook and share. The private module does not replace it for groups. Leave it clean (see <a href="/en/casa/limpeza/">Cleaning</a>) and return tableware to the space where you took it (see <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a>).</p>
<h2 id="forno">Large oven and dishwasher</h2>
<p>The large oven is inefficient for everyday cooking. It does not make sense to turn it on for a few people. Keep the large oven for large events. The same rule applies to the dishwasher.</p>
<p>The everyday alternative — what to use instead of the large oven — is not decided yet: ${pending}</p>
<h2>Shopping and pantry</h2>
<ul>
<li>For day to day, organise your own shopping (nearby towns / local shops).</li>
<li>If you arrive outside shop hours, bring food. See the <a href="/en/como-chegar/#pack-de-chegada">arrival pack</a>.</li>
<li>MuiGastromenta workshops have an <strong>operating shopping fund</strong> managed by the connector. It is not a personal pantry.</li>
<li>Bread and fish days, the nearest supermarket, and home delivery: <a href="/en/vida-diaria/mobilidade/#servizos">Getting around</a>.</li>
</ul>`,
	},
	'vida-diaria/mobilidade': {
		title: 'Getting around',
		description: 'Moving around Muimenta, shops, places of interest, and what is still unconfirmed.',
		body: `<p class="lede">The village is small and walkable. Towns and services need a plan.</p>
<h2>In the village</h2>
<ul>
<li>The project spaces are a short walk apart.</li>
<li>On arrival for a stay, unload at the module and leave the car at the social centre or the palco. See <a href="/en/como-chegar/">Getting here</a>.</li>
<li>At events, use the <strong>water tank</strong> car park.</li>
<li>Respect paths, gardens and private property.</li>
