	'vida-diaria/muigastromenta': {
		title: 'MuiGastromenta',
		description: 'Community cooking gatherings led by neighbours in Muimenta.',
		body: `<p class="lede">A periodic gathering in the community kitchen: a neighbour proposes and leads a recipe or workshop, and people cook and spend time together with no barrier to entry.</p>
<h2>What it is</h2>
<p><strong>MuiGastromenta</strong> takes its spirit from the «café da fresca»: a lively, periodic format for cohesion between neighbours and people from outside. It is not a restaurant and not a formal course. It is cooking and conversation.</p>
<h2>How it works</h2>
<ul>
<li>A <strong>neighbour leads</strong> the recipe or the workshop.</li>
<li>It happens in the <strong>community kitchen</strong>.</li>
<li>The connector handles logistics and an <strong>operating shopping fund</strong> for basic ingredients.</li>
<li>Related supplier invoices are issued to <strong>Sende</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>If you are a resident</h2>
<ul>
<li>Join when there is a gathering: it is one of the best doors into the community.</li>
<li>Follow the pace of the person leading. Offer help without taking over.</li>
<li>Do not publish photos of people without explicit permission.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Calendar:</strong> the exact frequency is set on the ground. Ask Lucía what is on during your stay.</div>`,
	},
	'residencias/modelo': {
		title: 'Residency model',
		description: 'Temporary residencies in the activation phase, and the host’s minimum of 1 hour a week.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Temporary stays to create and be present in the territory, in the activation phase — distinct from the connector’s role.</p>
<h2>Activation phase</h2>
<p>This is not a finished co-living. Few people live here day to day. A one-off profile or an urban practice is not the same as co-living life. There are too few people for this to be a co-living, and too much social mediation for it to be an artistic residency. We are careful with the language so we do not promise what is not yet in place.</p>
<h2>What it is (and is not)</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Temporary residencies</strong> are creative stays (usually one or two weeks, depending on the rules and capacity) to develop a project in the place.</li>
<li>They are <strong>unpaid</strong>, and the frame is different from the project connector, who lives the day to day and holds coordination and communication.</li>
<li>As an operating rule, we prioritise <strong>one person or group at a time</strong>, according to space and the team’s load.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Hosts and mutual learning</h2>
<p>Each resident can have a <strong>local host</strong>: a neighbour who, depending on the season, invites you to learn real tasks (garden, grape harvest, household knowledge).</p>
<p>In the programme rules the commitment is a <strong>minimum of 1 hour a week</strong>. It is not “daily tasks”. In practice it is always more, because the relationship happens in daily life — we say it this way so the expectation stays honest. The written minimum is that hour.</p>
<ul>
<li>The focus is <strong>practical learning</strong>, not only theory about rural life.</li>
<li>Neighbours want to share what they know how to do. Respect their time and limits.</li>
<li>It is an exchange: you bring your craft; they bring the lived territory.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Deliverables and care for the territory</h2>
<ul>
<li>Work with a <strong>concrete project</strong> and clear deliverables, agreed at the start.</li>
<li>If your work touches memories, stories or images of people, publish only with <strong>consent</strong>.</li>
<li>Materials that stay in the village should be respectful and useful for the community.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Coordination</h2>
<p>Residencies are coordinated with the connector and with <strong>Sende</strong> and <strong>Anceu</strong>. Before dates are fixed there is an <a href="/en/residencias/expectativas/">expectations video call</a> (dates, deliverables, and whether the project fits). The team can pace new residencies: dates are not automatic.</p>`,
	},
	'residencias/expectativas': {
		title: 'Expectations',
		description: 'What the project offers, what it asks, and the video call before the stay.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Mutual clarity before you arrive: what the project offers, what it asks, and what we close on the video call.</p>
<p>This is the expectations page. The project is in the <a href="/en/residencias/modelo/">activation phase</a>: read what follows as what is real today, not as the promise of a finished co-living.</p>
<h2>What the project offers</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lodging</strong> in the spaces of the agreement.</li>
<li><strong>Orientation</strong> on arrival (keys, a walk through the spaces, a contact person).</li>
<li>A <strong>host</strong>, when there is one: a minimum of 1 hour a week in the rules, not daily tasks. In practice it is always more. See <a href="/en/residencias/modelo/">The model</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Kitchen and spaces</strong> agreed for living together and working. See <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a>.</li>
<li>A <strong>coordination channel</strong> with the team (project WhatsApp / Lucía).</li>
</ul>
<p>Clear frame: you will not be asked to take on institutional commitments outside the residency. If someone wants a yes in the project’s name, the answer is “I will check with the team and get back to you.”</p>
<h2>What the project asks</h2>
<ul>
<li>A <strong>concrete project</strong>, not only an abstract intention.</li>
<li>Flexibility to join what is already happening <strong>without imposing an agenda</strong> on the village.</li>
<li>Respect for the <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">co-living</a> agreements and the spaces.</li>
<li>Fluid communication with your contact person.</li>
<li><strong>Explicit consent</strong> before publishing photos or videos of people.</li>
<li>Your own board during the stay (according to the call rules).</li>
<li>The <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">first-day agreements</a>: shared life, neighbours’ privacy, and the rhythm of the house.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Video call beforehand</h2>
<p>Before dates are closed we do a <strong>video call</strong> to align three things: dates, deliverables, and whether the project fits this phase (compatibility with the house and the village). If something does not fit, say it there.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Capacity:</strong> the team can pace new residencies to protect day-to-day stability and to prioritise community events. Dates are not automatic.</div>`,
	},
	comunidade: {
		title: 'Community',
		description: 'What we usually do, and operational neutrality in Muimenta Viva.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Bringing the village to life means weaving trust: real gatherings, shared cooking, and a careful presence in the territory.</p>
<h2>What we seek</h2>
<p>Muimenta Viva works on <strong>social, gastronomic and entrepreneurial</strong> activation. Gatherings are short, concrete, and meant so neighbours and people from outside meet in the rehabilitated spaces.</p>
<h2>What we usually do</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>MuiGastromenta</strong> — community cooking led by neighbours (<a href="/en/vida-diaria/muigastromenta/">more</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Community gatherings</strong> — guided visits, vermouth, workshops and cultural pieces at a human scale.</li>
<li><strong>Residencies</strong> — a temporary presence that activates spaces and leaves deliverables in the place (<a href="/en/residencias/modelo/">the model</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Meetings and networking</strong> — with related programmes and networks, always coordinated with the team.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Operational neutrality</h2>
<p>The project keeps an <strong>operational neutrality</strong> toward disputes outside the agreement. Before committing to anything — visits, workshops, deals with third parties — check with the team. The agreed line is:</p>
<blockquote><p>“I will check with the team and get back to you.”</p></blockquote>
<p>This protects trust with local people and stops one person from committing the whole (Sende, Anceu, the connector and the institutional frame).</p>
<h2>Communication</h2>
<ul>
<li>Daily channel: project WhatsApp / Lucía.</li>
<li>Internal documentation: the team’s coordination board.</li>
<li>Public materials: include Xunta / Consellería de Emprego branding when the event or the poster represents the project.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Calendar:</strong> this wiki does not list a live calendar with personal names and dates. For what is on during your stay, ask the connector.</div>`,
	},
	equipo: {
		title: 'Team and partnerships',
		description: 'Who coordinates Muimenta Viva, and who we work with.',
		body: `<p class="lede">Who makes things happen on the ground, and who the project is built with.</p>
<h2>On the ground</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Lucía Fernández Abuchdid</strong> — connector: day to day in the village, digital communication, bridge with neighbours, and logistics of gatherings.</li></ul>
<h2>Coordination</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sende</strong> — project coordination, operating frame, and part of the administration of events and suppliers.</li>
<li><strong>Anceu Coliving</strong> — coordination and the residency network / learning from co-living models.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Institutional frame and partnerships</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Consellería de Emprego, Comercio e Emigración</strong> (Xunta de Galicia) — the agreement frame and institutional visibility on public materials.</li>
<li><strong>Concello de Carballeda de Avia</strong> — host council and local interlocutor for spaces and services.</li>
<li><strong>Fundación Ría</strong> — a reference in the rehabilitation process and a territorial gaze.</li>
</ul>
<p>Working with Sende and Anceu means Muimenta Viva is not an isolated initiative: it is part of a network of spaces that learn from each other.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Contact:</strong> for residencies and on-the-ground coordination, write through the channels on the project website, or via the connector once the stay is confirmed.</div>
<div class="team-only"><p><strong>Team.</strong> Internal follow-up of resident feedback (shower, fridges, tableware, profiles and priorities) is in <a href="/en/equipo/melloras/">Improvements in progress</a>. That page is not the resident guide.</p></div>`,
	},
	'equipo/melloras': {
		title: 'Improvements in progress',
		description: 'Internal follow-up of resident feedback. Not the guide for people staying in Muimenta.',
		body: `<div class="team-only"><p><strong>This page is for the team.</strong> It records resident feedback from the document “Mejoras con Mojar” (8 October 2026). It is not the co-living guide. Residents use <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">Co-living</a>, <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a> and <a href="/en/residencias/expectativas/">Expectations</a>.</p></div>
<h2>Frame</h2>
<ul>
<li>Feedback from conversations with residents, in this activation phase.</li>
<li>Aim: better shared life, a clearer programme, spaces and infrastructure.</li>
<li>Premise: we are still building; this is not yet a full co-living.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Residency profiles</h2>
<p>The programme carries a lot of social and mediation weight, because of demand from neighbours. That fits mediation and collaborative practice, and it pulls attention away from a “pure” artistic residency.</p>
<p>Proposal: diversify profiles, and ideally have several at once (cultural and productive):</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mediation / collaborative.</strong></li>
<li><strong>An anthropological gaze.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Agro / hands-on</strong> — clearing, woodland, territory.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Gender observation</strong> (from the feedback, not a rule for residents): cultural activity “gives back” more to women; return toward the men of the village is missing. A male presence drew more men.</div>
<h2>Module shower</h2>
<ul>
<li>Water seeps underneath; a stop is missing.</li>
<li>Hypothesis from the feedback: silicone is missing on the tray. Not verified.</li>
<li>The wet area is permanent and may be the source of the smell.</li>
<li>Action: review and repair, as a priority.</li>
</ul>
<p>The resident guide only has a practical note (say if it gets worse), in <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a> and <a href="/en/casa/limpeza/">Cleaning</a>.</p>
<h2>Kitchen: large oven and dishwasher</h2>
<ul>
<li>The large oven is inefficient for everyday use. So is the dishwasher.</li>
<li>It does not make sense to turn them on for a few people. They are useful above all at large events.</li>
<li>The use rule (yes for large events, no for an ordinary day with few people) is in <a href="/en/vida-diaria/comidas/#forno">Food</a>.</li>
<li>The everyday alternative is not chosen yet: ${pending}</li>
</ul>
<h2>Fridges and storage (upper floor)</h2>
<p>A detected need, not equipment that is already there:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Coworking</strong> (the windowed building): a small fridge.</li>
<li><strong>Social centre / upper floor</strong> (the two-storey building): a large fridge with a freezer, able to sit inside the cupboards.</li>
<li>Reason: more activity upstairs and events of 30–60 people.</li>
<li>More glasses, cups, plates and storage are also needed upstairs.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Duplicated tableware</h2>
<ul>
<li>Dishes currently go up and down, and pieces are missing in one space or the other.</li>
<li>Have a basic set duplicated in the community kitchen and on the upper floor.</li>
</ul>
<p>The practical note for residents (return tableware to where it was taken) is in <a href="/en/casa/espazos/">Spaces</a>.</p>
<h2>Priorities</h2>
<p>The order comes from the feedback. What is already written in the guide is linked; building work and purchases stay open.</p>
<h3>Now / urgent</h3>
<ol>
<li>Repair the module shower and the smell. Building work still open.</li>
<li>Module visit protocol. Written in <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/#visitas-modulos">Co-living</a>.</li>
<li>Wiki corrections: coworking = the windows, social centre = two floors, and “What we usually do” instead of “formats that repeat”. Done in the guide. The gathering name stays <strong>MuiGastromenta</strong> (that is how the repo spells it; «café da fresca» was already right). Map and shops still have no data.</li>
<li>Host expectation (minimum 1 hour a week) and activation phase. Written in <a href="/en/">The project</a>, <a href="/en/residencias/modelo/">The model</a> and <a href="/en/residencias/expectativas/">Expectations</a>.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Short term</h3>
<ol>
<li>Small fridge in the coworking and large fridge with freezer on the upper floor. Purchase still open.</li>
<li>Duplicated tableware. Purchase still open.</li>
<li>Arrival pack and leaving checklist. Written in <a href="/en/como-chegar/#pack-de-chegada">Getting here</a> and <a href="/en/antes-de-irte/">Before you leave</a>. Sheets, towels, bicycle and animals still carry a marker.</li>
<li>Large-oven use rule. Written in <a href="/en/vida-diaria/comidas/#forno">Food</a>. The everyday alternative is still pending.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Medium term / programming</h3>
<ol>
<li>Diversify residency profiles: mediation, agro, or mixed.</li>
<li>Activities that also give something back to the men of the village.</li>
</ol>
<p>Back to <a href="/en/equipo/">Team and partnerships</a>.</p>`,
	},
	'antes-de-irte': {
		title: 'Before you leave',
		description: 'Leaving checklist for the end of a Muimenta Viva stay.',
		body: `<p class="lede">A short list to close the stay: spaces, keys, deliverables, and how to stay in touch afterwards.</p>
<h2>Leaving checklist</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Clean the module and the shared spaces</strong> you used (community kitchen, upper floor, coworking…).</li>
<li><strong>Return the keys</strong> to the connector or to whoever the team names.</li>
<li><strong>Hand over the agreed deliverables</strong>, in the format and place you were given.</li>
<li><strong>Review publications and consent.</strong> Photos and videos of people only with explicit permission.</li>
<li><strong>Leave brief feedback</strong> — a conversation or a note. It helps the next stay.</li>
<li><strong>Take your belongings and your food</strong> from the pantry and the rooms.</li>
<li><strong>Say the exact time you are leaving.</strong></li>
<li><strong>If you want to stay in touch</strong>, leave a channel agreed with the team, without flooding the neighbours.</li>
</ol>
<p>Thank you for inhabiting Muimenta with presence and care. The activation phase is built stay by stay.</p>
<p>See also: <a href="/en/casa/limpeza/">Cleaning</a> · <a href="/en/casa/convivencia/">Co-living</a>.</p>`,
	},
};

